# en -> fr

#: application/dicom
msgid "DICOM"
msgstr "DICOM"

#: application/dicom@definition
msgid "Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) MIME type defined in RFC3240 \\[http://ietf.org/rfc/rfc3240.txt\\]."
msgstr ""

#: application/msword
msgid "MSWORD"
msgstr "MSWORD"

#: application/msword@definition
msgid "This format is very prone to compatibility problems. If sharing of edit-able text is required, text/plain, text/html or text/rtf should be used instead."
msgstr ""

#: application/pdf
msgid "PDF"
msgstr "PDF"

#: application/pdf@definition
msgid "The Portable Document Format is recommended for written text that is completely laid out and read-only. PDF is a platform independent, widely deployed, and open specification with freely available creation and rendering tools."
msgstr ""

#: audio/basic
msgid "Basic Audio"
msgstr "Basic Audio"

#: audio/basic@definition
msgid "This is a format for single channel audio, encoded using 8bit ISDN mu-law \\[PCM\\] at a sample rate of 8000 Hz. This format is standardized by: CCITT, Fascicle III.4 -Recommendation G.711. Pulse Code Modulation (PCM) of Voice Frequencies. Geneva, 1972."
msgstr ""

#: audio/k32adpcm
msgid "K32ADPCM Audio"
msgstr "K32ADPCM Audio"

#: audio/k32adpcm@definition
msgid "ADPCM allows compressing audio data. It is defined in the Internet specification RFC 2421 \\[ftp://ftp.isi.edu/in-notes/rfc2421.txt\\]. Its implementation base is unclear."
msgstr ""

#: audio/mpeg
msgid "MPEG audio layer 3"
msgstr "MPEG audio layer 3 MP3 Audio"

#: audio/mpeg@definition
msgid "MPEG-1 Audio layer-3 is an audio compression algorithm and file format defined in ISO 11172-3 and ISO 13818-3. MP3 has an adjustable sampling frequency for highly compressed telephone to CD quality audio."
msgstr ""

#: image/gif
msgid "GIF Image"
msgstr "GIF Image"

#: image/gif@definition
msgid "GIF is a popular format that is universally well supported. However GIF is patent encumbered and should therefore be used with caution."
msgstr ""

#: image/jpeg
msgid "JPEG Image"
msgstr "JPEG Image"

#: image/jpeg@definition
msgid "This format is required for high compression of high color photographs. It is a \"lossy\" compression, but the difference to lossless compression is almost unnoticeable to the human vision."
msgstr ""

#: image/png
msgid "PNG Image"
msgstr "PNG Image"

#: image/png@definition
msgid "Portable Network Graphics (PNG) \\[http://www.cdrom.com/pub/png\\] is a widely supported lossless image compression standard with open source code available."
msgstr ""

#: image/tiff
msgid "TIFF Image"
msgstr "TIFF Image"

#: image/tiff@definition
msgid "Although TIFF (Tag Image File Format) is an international standard it has many interoperability problems in practice. Too many different versions that are not handled by all software alike."
msgstr ""

#: text/html
msgid "HTML Text"
msgstr "HTML Text"

#: text/html@definition
msgid "For marked-up text according to the Hypertext Mark-up Language. HTML markup is sufficient for typographically marking-up most written-text documents. HTML is platform independent and widely deployed."
msgstr ""

#: text/plain
msgid "Plain Text"
msgstr "Plain Text"

#: text/plain@definition
msgid "**Description:**For any plain text. This is the default and is used for a character string (ST) data type."
msgstr ""

#: text/rtf
msgid "RTF Text"
msgstr "RTF Text"

#: text/rtf@definition
msgid "The Rich Text Format is widely used to share word-processor documents. However, RTF does have compatibility problems, as it is quite dependent on the word processor. May be useful if word processor edit-able text should be shared."
msgstr ""

#: text/xml
msgid "XML Text"
msgstr "XML Text"

#: text/xml@definition
msgid "For structured character based data. There is a risk that general SGML/XML is too powerful to allow a sharing of general SGML/XML documents between different applications."
msgstr ""
